#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1392
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remarks Regarding the Samba Security Fixes of April 12, 2016"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1393
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On April 12, 2016 the Samba team released security fixes for the <ulink url="
"\"http://www.badlock.org\">Badlock bug</ulink>. Unfortunately, they also "
"introduced a regression that causes the <command>net</command> command to "
"fail on many systems when querying remote hosts. If you experience this "
"issue, you can add two lines to the [global] section of your <filename>smb."
"conf</filename> file to make browsing work again:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: programlisting
#: index.docbook:1394
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"[global]\n"
"    ...\n"
"    client max protocol = SMB3\n"
"    client ipc max protocol = NT1\n"
"    ..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1395
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, this fix for &smb4k; breaks the possibility to connect to the "
"network neighborhood with &dolphin; and maybe also other programs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1401
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remarks for FreeBSD Users"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1404
#, no-c-format
msgid "DBUS and PolKit-1"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1405
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&smb4k; makes use of the &kde; authorization API (KAuth) to enable mounting "
"of remote shares. KAuth uses DBUS and PolKit-1 (or PolicyKit) for privilege "
"escalation, so it is necessary that &smb4k; is set up properly. When "
"installing &smb4k; under FreeBSD, it might be necessary to manually adjust "
"some things to achieve this (With version 1.0.10 of package "
"<application>kdehier4</application> this seems to be fixed!):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1408
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check that the file <filename>net.sourceforge.smb4k.mounthelper.policy</"
"filename> exists in the directory <filename class=\"directory\">/usr/local/"
"share/polkit-1/actions/</filename>. If it is not present, you need to link "
"(or copy) it to that location:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1409
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><prompt>$</prompt> <command>cd</command> <filename class="
"\"directory\">/usr/local/share/polkit-1/actions/</filename></userinput>\n"
"<userinput><prompt>$</prompt> <command>sudo ln</command> -s \\\n"
"<filename>/usr/local/kde4/share/polkit-1/actions/net.sourceforge.smb4k."
"mounthelper.policy</filename> .</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1412
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The installation most likely put the DBUS files into the wrong location, so "
"you have to link (or copy) them to the right one:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1413
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><prompt>$</prompt> <command>cd</command> <filename class="
"\"directory\">/usr/local/share/dbus-1/system-services</filename></"
"userinput>\n"
"<userinput><prompt>$</prompt> <command>sudo ln</command> -s \\\n"
"<filename>/usr/local/kde4/share/dbus-1/system-services/net.sourceforge.smb4k."
"mounthelper.service</filename> .</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1419
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mounting of Shares (Smb4K >= 1.2.0)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1420
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since version 1.2.0, the password for a share is directly passed to "
"<command>mount_smbfs</command>, so that the <filename>~/.nsmbrc</filename> "
"is not necessary anymore for mounting to work. Moreover, &smb4k; will not "
"write any data to that file anymore."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1427
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remarks for NetBSD Users"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1430
#, no-c-format
msgid "DBUS and PolicyKit"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1431
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Under NetBSD, &smb4k; is able to run since version 1.2.0. However, some "
"modifications have to be made in order to be able to mount and unmount "
"shares:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1432
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Assuming that the prefix of your &kde; installation is <filename class="
"\"directory\">/usr/pkg</filename>, the following steps have to be taken to "
"make &smb4k; work properly:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1434
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Configure, compile and install &smb4k; according to the directions given in "
"the <link linkend=\"appendix_compilation\">Configuration, Compilation and "
"Installation</link> section of the appendix."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1435
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After installation, link (or copy) the file <filename>net.sourceforge.smb4k."
"mounthelper.conf</filename> from the <filename class=\"directory\">examples</"
"filename> directory to the right location:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1436
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<userinput><prompt>$</prompt> <command>cd</command> <filename class="
"\"directory\">/usr/pkg/etc/dbus-1/system.d/</filename></userinput>\n"
"<userinput><prompt>$</prompt> <command>sudo ln</command> -s \\\n"
"<filename>/usr/pkg/share/examples/kde4-dbus/net.sourceforge.smb4k."
"mounthelper.conf</filename> .</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1437
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Edit the file <filename>/usr/pkg/etc/PolicyKit/PolicyKit.conf</filename> and "
"add the following paragraph in the &lt;config version=\"0.1\"&gt; section:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:1438
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&lt;match action=\"net.sourceforge.smb4k.mounthelper.*\"&gt;\n"
"        &lt;return result=\"yes\"&gt;\n"
"&lt;/match&gt;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1439
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will allow everyone to mount and unmount remote Samba shares with "
"&smb4k;."
msgstr ""

